Most of them are not very useful, but you must clear the Level 3 contest in order to obtain a mandatory plot item.  And the Sage's Stone is every bit as useful as it sounds; in fact, it is almost mandatory for beating the final boss without high levels or the Hero job class.

However, going past Level 4 is not feasible yet.  This is because there are hidden point bonuses that come with certain combinations of equipment; and unfortunately, the later levels rely heavily on bonuses that can only come from end-game weapons and armor.  For now, the only high-end point bonuses you can get are:

<blockquote>
50+ from Bunny Suit + Silver Platter + Bunny Ears + Fishnet Stockings

40+ from Miracle Sword + Sacred Armour

35+ from Lunar Fan + Dancer's Costume
</blockquote>

Fortunately, you can also equip the Turnscote Pendant for an incredibly high +40 boost in Style; combine that with the +133 total boost from the Miracle Sword + Sacred Armour, and that should be more than enough for Carver or Rex to sweep Levels 1-3.  And if you kept all of the Bunny equipment, you can sweep Level 4 with Milly as well.

If you haven't been following the guide, and do not have the Miracle Sword or Sacred Armour, you can still win.  The Platinum Shield, Platinum Mail, Helm of Sebath, and Turnscote Pendant are all high Style items that are impossible to lose and easy to acquire, so just refer to the [[Dragon Quest VI: Realms of Revelation/Item collection: Part 2|Item collection: Part 2]], [[Dragon Quest VI: Realms of Revelation/Helm of Sebath|Helm of Sebath (VS. Man-at-Arms)]], and [[Dragon Quest VI: Realms of Revelation/Sword of Ramias|Sword of Ramias]] pages to find all those.

== Well of Somnia (Real World) ==

[[File:DQ6 Somnia's Well (RW).png|thumb|right|]]

[[File:DQ6 Path to Somnian Well (RW).jpg|thumb|left|]]

This is an optional excursion for the [[File:Dragon Warrior 3 SNES Small Medal.png]] <span style="color:green">72nd Mini Medal</span> and a shield that casts Midheal upon use. To get in, sail your ship through the river to Somnia and dive underwater to find a cave opening. After that, you will want to stop by Medford Medallion's and get the Metal King Helm.  This powerful helm reduces the wearer 3/4 resistance to all status and death spells; so pick it up if you can. 




== Extra Seed of Magic (Cole's Grave) ==

[[File:DQ6 Seed of Magic at Cole's Grave.png|thumb|right]]

[[File:DQ6 Path to Cole's Grave.jpg|thumb|left]]

As the name of the section implies, this is the site of Cole's death.  There is no hope of closure for him and his family now; but you can still use the Seed of Magic in forging a future for his daughter.  Use it on Rex if you are following the guide's suggestions.

Whatever you decide, this is the end of the Item Collection segments; it's now finally time to tackle the Seabed Shrine.  '''Change Goowain into a Martial Artist''', and make sure to reform your party to look something like the below before you do; this next dungeon is very long, so an all-melee party is more helpful in this case:

